      "function": {
        "name": "choose_adsorption_site_text",
        "description": "Fractional coordinates of the selected adsorption site.\n\nA list of three floating-point numbers representing the fractional coordinates [x, y, z] of the selected adsorption site within the unit cell.\n                These coordinates can be used directly for adsorbate placement and represent the optimal binding position for the specified site type.\n\nWhen to use: When to use this tool:\n- Use after identifying all possible adsorption site to select a specific binding site\n- Best suited for systematic comparison of different site types\n- Essential for placing adsorbates at specific coordination environments\n- Recommended when studying site-specific reactivity or selectivity\n- Avoid when you need to place adsorbates at multiple sites simultaneously\n\nHow this tool works:\n- Parses the JSON string containing classified adsorption sites\n- Locates the specified site type in the dictionary\n- Selects the site at the specified index within that type\n- Returns the fractional coordinates as a list of three floats\n\nWorkflow: Typical workflow integration example:\n1.  First run get_adsorption_sites_text to identify available sites \n2.  Apply this tool to select a specific site by type and index \n3.  Use the coordinates with add_adsorbate_to_slab_text for molecule placement",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "adsorption_sites_json": {
              "description": "JSON string mapping site types to lists of fractional coordinates. A JSON-formatted string containing a dictionary where keys are site types (e.g., \"ontop\", \"bridge\", \"hollow\") and values are lists of fractional coordinates. This should be the output from get_adsorption_sites_text. Each coordinate is a list of three numbers representing position within the unit cell.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "site_type": {
              "description": "Type of adsorption site to select. The type of binding site to select from the available options. Common types include \"ontop\" (above surface atoms), \"bridge\" (between two atoms), and  \"hollow\" (in multi-atom depressions). The type must exist in the JSON dictionary and determines the coordination environment of the selected site.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "index": {
              "description": "Index of the site within the specified type. Defaults to 0. The numerical index of the site to select from the list of sites of the specified type. Index 0 selects the first site, index 1 the second, and so on. The index must be within the range of available sites for the specified type.",
              "type": "integer",
              "default": 0
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "adsorption_sites_json",
            "site_type"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
